@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-06-09

Feature: Share Upload Dedupe Decision
  "Pure logic deciding whether share must noop, create, or repoint and whether blob bytes must upload."

  Provides:
    - domain.ShareAction @source("symbol:ShareAction")
    - domain.ShareDecision @source("symbol:ShareDecision")
    - domain.Manifest.DecideShare @source("symbol:DecideShare")

  Consumes:
    - domain.Manifest
    - domain.Manifest.FindShareByPath

  Invariants:
    - DecideShare MUST perform no I/O; blob presence is read only from the manifest blobs map
    - ShareNoop MUST apply when the object path already points at the same blob
    - ShareCreate MUST set UploadBlob false when the blob already exists remotely
    - ShareRepoint MUST record OldBlob for GC eligibility tracking

  Scenario (happy-path): Link-only new path
    Given a manifest where the blob exists but the object path is new
    When DecideShare runs
    Then Action is ShareCreate and UploadBlob is false

  Scenario (happy-path): No-op same content
    Given a manifest where the object path already references the same blob
    When DecideShare runs
    Then Action is ShareNoop and UploadBlob is false

  Scenario (happy-path): Repoint changed content
    Given a manifest where the object path references a different blob and the new blob is absent
    When DecideShare runs
    Then Action is ShareRepoint, UploadBlob is true, and OldBlob is set
